        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "19-4 A teacher may exclude a pupil from one (1) class period or session and refer such student to the principal or assistant principal consistent with the school discipline plan. In such cases, the teacher will furnish the principal or his/her designee, as promptly as his/her teaching obligation allows, full particulars of the incident in writing. However, every effort will be made by the teacher to submit to the principal or his/her designee the full particulars of the incident in writing by the end of the teacher's workday. The principal or his/her designee will respond in writing to teachers in a timely manner (normally within 24 hours) regarding such written disciplinary referrals. Every effort will be made by the principal or his/her designee to communicate with the teacher prior to the student's return to class.",
            "block_bbox": [
                36,
